# Cloudflare Pages consumes this file and does not serve it.
#
# There is deliberately no `X-Robots-Tag` block here. The IFO product site has
# one until that app launches; this site is the company's public identity and
# must be findable. See the comment at the top of index.html.
#
# The page has no scripts, no external assets and no forms, so the policy that
# describes it exactly is also the strictest one available. If an external
# asset is ever added — a font, an analytics tag, an embedded video — it will
# be blocked until the policy below is widened, which is the intended order of
# events rather than an obstacle.
#
# Comments sit outside the rule block on purpose: every non-comment line inside
# one is parsed as `Name: value`, and a malformed header there fails quietly.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; img-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()

# The `no-transform` below exists because Cloudflare rewrites the HTML it
# serves, and nothing else in this repo would record that it does.
#
# Two edge features have already modified this page in ways the source cannot
# show. Email Address Obfuscation rewrote the `mailto:` in index.html into a
# `/cdn-cgi/` link plus a decode script; JavaScript Detections injects an
# inline script into every HTML response. The policy above allows no scripts
# at all, so both were blocked — and the blocked decode script left the
# contact address rendering as the literal text "[email protected]" on the
# live site while `site/index.html` still looked perfectly correct. JSD
# injection also strips the ETag from the HTML response, so every repeat
# visit re-transfers the whole body instead of revalidating.
#
# `no-transform` tells Cloudflare to leave these responses alone. It is a fix
# that lives in the source tree rather than in a dashboard toggle, which
# matters here: a zone setting is invisible to anyone reading this repo and
# does not survive rebuilding the zone. Scoped to the HTML, because that is
# all Cloudflare injects into — style.css and mark.svg keep the longer
# max-age Pages gives them.
#
# The general lesson, which cost a working contact address to learn: verify
# the SERVED page, not the source. `curl` the live URL with a cache-busting
# query string and diff it against `site/`.

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, no-transform

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, no-transform
